                    <h2 class="text-3xl text-primary mt-12 mb-5" style="font-family: 'Bauhaus Soft', cursive;">Breaking Down the 5 Most Common Side Effects</h2>
                    
                    <h3 class="text-2xl text-primary mt-8 mb-4 font-semibold">1. Scalp Discomfort or Mild Pain</h3>
                    <p>The most common side effect reported by patients is mild to moderate scalp discomfort at the treatment site.</p>
                    <p>Because TMS uses magnetic pulses to stimulate nerve cells, the muscles and tissues in the scalp also receive some residual stimulation.</p>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 py-1">
                        <li><strong>What to expect:</strong> You will feel a tapping or clicking sensation on your head. For sensitive scalps, this can cause temporary discomfort during the first few minutes.</li>
                        <li><strong>How it's managed:</strong> This discomfort typically lessens significantly after the first week due to habituation. Our technicians can also make micro-adjustments to the coil position to maximize your comfort.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="text-2xl text-primary mt-8 mb-4 font-semibold">2. Tension Headaches</h3>
                    <p>Headaches are another very frequently reported, yet highly manageable, side effect of TMS therapy.</p>
                    <p>Clinical data suggests that roughly half of all patients will experience a mild headache following a treatment session, particularly during the first week.</p>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 py-1">
                        <li><strong>What to expect:</strong> These headaches mimic a standard tension headache rather than a migraine. They usually begin shortly after the session ends.</li>
                        <li><strong>How it's managed:</strong> Over-the-counter pain medication (like ibuprofen) is typically sufficient. Drinking water and applying a warm compress to the neck also provide significant relief.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="text-2xl text-primary mt-8 mb-4 font-semibold">3. Facial Muscle Twitching</h3>
                    <p>The magnetic pulses inevitably stimulate the superficial nerves located in the scalp and face.</p>
                    <p>This can occasionally cause temporary tingling, spasms, or involuntary twitching of the facial muscles.</p>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 py-1">
                        <li><strong>What to expect:</strong> You might notice a slight, rhythmic twitch in your jaw or eyebrow that corresponds with the tapping of the machine.</li>
                        <li><strong>How it's managed:</strong> This is harmless and stops the moment the machine turns off. If it is uncomfortable, your technician can adjust the coil placement slightly.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="text-2xl text-primary mt-8 mb-4 font-semibold">4. Mild Lightheadedness</h3>
                    <p>A small percentage of patients report feeling lightheaded or dizzy during or immediately following a session.</p>
                    <p>This is often a physiological response to the new sensation or minor anxiety about the procedure.</p>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 py-1">
                        <li><strong>What to expect:</strong> This sensation is usually brief, mild in nature, and resolves entirely on its own within a few minutes.</li>
                        <li><strong>How it's managed:</strong> We encourage patients to remain seated until they feel grounded. Having a light snack before your appointment can also help prevent dizziness.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="text-2xl text-primary mt-8 mb-4 font-semibold">5. Temporary Alterations in Hearing</h3>
                    <p>The TMS machine generates a loud clicking noise during operation.</p>
                    <p>Because the coil is placed near the ear, this acoustic noise can be quite loud without protection.</p>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 border-l-4 border-accent pl-4 py-1">
                        <li><strong>What to expect:</strong> Without protection, you might experience temporary ringing in the ears or muffled hearing.</li>
                        <li><strong>How it's managed:</strong> We provide high-quality earplugs for every single session. You are also welcome to listen to music through earbuds to block out the sound.</li>
                    </ul>

