                    <h2 class="text-3xl text-primary mt-12 mb-5" style="font-family: 'Bauhaus Soft', cursive;">Rare but Serious Risks: The Risk of Seizures</h2>
                    <p>While extremely rare, the most serious potential side effect of TMS therapy is the induction of a generalized seizure.</p>
                    <p>The overall risk is estimated to be less than 0.1% per treatment course. This risk is actually lower than or comparable to the risk associated with some oral antidepressants.</p>
                    <p>To eliminate this risk, our psychiatric providers conduct a rigorous medical history review before approving you for treatment. Individuals with a history of epilepsy or traumatic brain injuries may not be candidates.</p>

